    "Part four. The long march.",
    "Taking one territory is nice. But the turns that win games are the ones where you tear through three, four, five territories in a row.",
    "Every time you win, you have to leave one army behind. So your stack shrinks with every step.",
    "So we started with ten armies and marched through territories with one defender each.",
    "The first three are almost guaranteed. Then it starts to fade.",
    "Territory five, 78 percent. Territory six, about a coin flip. Territory eight, almost never.",
    "On average, ten armies take about 5.6 territories.",
    "Now put two defenders on every territory. Ten armies take just 3.2 on average.",
    "That second defender doesn't just slow you down. It cuts your march almost in half.",
    "Double your stack to twenty armies, and against two defenders each, you take about 7.1.",
    "And here's the defensive lesson. If you know someone is about to march through you, two armies per territory is the cheapest wall in the game.",
    "Write that one down. And tell me in the comments: are you the player who marches, or the one who builds the wall?"
